# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform.
#
# This checkout has core.autocrlf=true. A .sh file given CRLF endings and then copied into a Linux
# image fails with `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`, which is a confusing way to learn about line
# endings at three in the morning when a backup does not run.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux tools inside containers.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
